orum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:44:45-07:00","id":123236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122566-mortal-remains-errata-thread?p=123019#post123019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P. 24: &quot;even when <b>were </b>together&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Original Text: </b>He never stopped looking for them, <b>even when were together</b> and there were no windows.<br /> <b>Proposed Change:</b> even when we were together","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 05-01-2014, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:48:37-07:00","id":123243,"title":"","content":"Page 24-25 (The Long Night)<br /> <br /> <b>Original Text: </b>In practice, the Long Night doesn\u2019t tend to find Prometheans that observe the Pilgrimage carefully.<br /> <br /> <b>Proposed Change: </b>In practice, the Long Night doesn\u2019t tend to find Prometheans that observe <b>their </b>Pilgrimage carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 05-01-2014, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T17:56:53-07:00","id":123529,"title":"","content":"Page 57 under Compound Rounds<br /> <br /> Function: Compound Rounds contain small amounts of<br /> just about any substance rumored to affect supernatural creatures:<br /> cold iron, gold, silver, salt, a variety of wood <b>silvers</b>,<br /> <br /> s<b>il</b>vers should be changed to s<b>li</b>vers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T22:10:42-07:00","id":123607,"title":"","content":"Page 149 in Dream Walking &quot;where the monster uses the <b>lower</b> of its Wits <b>+ </b>Resolve as a surrogate&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2881-zilchr0","name":"zilchr0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T03:28:09-07:00","id":123695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zilchr0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122566-mortal-remains-errata-thread?p=123607#post123607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 149 in Dream Walking &quot;where the monster uses the <b>lower</b> of its Wits <b>+ </b>Resolve as a surrogate&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the problem with this? What do you think it should be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T06:53:59-07:00","id":123753,"title":"","content":"p86, Naomi Redbord character sheet : Special attack : Firestarter : &quot;Naomi can spend a point of Willpower <b>to cause an object to cause an object</b> to catch fire.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2809-batro","name":"batro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:08:21-07:00","id":124131,"title":"","content":"Not sure if a real errata or an editorial decision: The Mummy chapter does not have a Systems section bulleting what special qualities Mummies have as innate abilities and weaknesses like the previous chapters do. I say this because in the absence of a quick start for the Mummy line and only one antagonist statted out, its a bit difficult to get a clear picture of their common powers and any weaknesses are without having access to the Mummy core. Narrative wise the chapter paints a thrilling picture but its very hazy on the details compared to other chapters that have botu the narrative and a quick reference for the systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:21:44-07:00","id":124140,"title":"","content":"Not a typo per se, but a bit of confusion all the same: the Unholy Aura Castigation on P.55 has an activation roll vs. Composure, but it doesn't say whose Composure it is. The power only says that the hunter's social dice pools are increased, not that they are increased against one particular opponent, If that's the case, then whose Composure is it, The hunter's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T02:52:58-07:00","id":124385,"title":"","content":"This is also not a typo, but just a little bit of cultural ignorance that seems to pop up in way too many depictions of modern day Egyptians in western media: the inclusion of ancient Egyptian words in modern day people's names. The specific example I'm citing here is the founder of Habibti Ma's name: Eme <b>Amun</b> Hassan. I'll let her given name slide since there's an actual person with that name, but even then she's Lebanese and the name is still extremely strange; but the middle name, which given the rules of Arabic nomenclature would be her father's name, is extremely odd by today's and even the not-so-recent past's standards. To put things in perspective, basically the only ancient Egyptian name you'll ever hear in today's Egypt is Mena (Menes), with maybe the occasional Ramsis every so often. Even then, those names are basically exclusively used by Christians, which Habibti Ma's founder doesn't seem to be.<br /> <br /> Another thing is Habibti Ma's name itself, which translates as &quot;my love (female) 'Ma'&quot;, which is pretty silly-sounding in Arabic. I'm guessing &quot;Ma&quot; is a shortening of Ma'at, since it's not an actual Arabic word.<br /> <br /> As an Egyptian and a native Arabic-speaker, it's always so jarring to see things like this when reading a WW book, since they usually seem well-researched when it comes to other cultures, so I'm hoping that the great writers of the Onyx Path take this into consideration in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T06:04:08-07:00","id":124432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122566-mortal-remains-errata-thread?p=124385#post124385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also not a typo, but just a little bit of cultural ignorance that seems to pop up in way too many depictions of modern day Egyptians in western media: the inclusion of ancient Egyptian words in modern day people's names. The specific example I'm citing here is the founder of Habibti Ma's name: Eme <b>Amun</b> Hassan. I'll let her given name slide since there's an actual person with that name, but even then she's Lebanese and the name is still extremely strange; but the middle name, which given the rules of Arabic nomenclature would be her father's name, is extremely odd by today's and even the not-so-recent past's standards. To put things in perspective, basically the only ancient Egyptian name you'll ever hear in today's Egypt is Mena (Menes), with maybe the occasional Ramsis every so often. Even then, those names are basically exclusively used by Christians, which Habibti Ma's founder doesn't seem to be.<br /> <br /> Another thing is Habibti Ma's name itself, which translates as &quot;my love (female) 'Ma'&quot;, which is pretty silly-sounding in Arabic. I'm guessing &quot;Ma&quot; is a shortening of Ma'at, since it's not an actual Arabic word.<br /> <br /> As an Egyptian and a native Arabic-speaker, it's always so jarring to see things like this when reading a WW book, since they usually seem well-researched when it comes to other cultures, so I'm hoping that the great writers of the Onyx Path take this into consideration in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a little weird. I asked an Egyptian Arabic speaker for her advice when this came up. Those names came from her input. <br /> <br /> It happens. Sorry it came off jarring for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T06:18:51-07:00","id":124441,"title":"","content":"Maybe language consultants should be vetted better, I found similar issues in <i>Shadows of Mexico</i>, some so jarringly wrong that whenever I read it its hard to ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T08:10:52-07:00","id":124507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122566-mortal-remains-errata-thread?p=124441#post124441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe language consultants should be vetted better, I found similar issues in <i>Shadows of Mexico</i>, some so jarringly wrong that whenever I read it its hard to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I don't know who worked on Shadows Of Mexico, or the offending sections in question. But when I'm doing something international, I do what I can to find a native, or someone well-versed. There's no complicated vetting process, because frankly, I'm not paid enough to put days of hard work into what amounts to a few paragraphs of work. It's hard enough talking to someone and waiting for an answer on 1,000 words when I need to write 4,000-5,000 a day to pay the bills. But hoping for a deep and considerable effort that spans days of effort for what amounts to $30 is just setting yourself up for disappointment. <br /> <br /> If I were doing a whole book on a topic, I try to find an expert. Then again, an expert usually demands (and reasonably so) a much higher rate than RPGs pay. <br /> <br /> Ironically, a common response in these things is, &quot;you could always just post on the forums asking&quot;. Which, as far as I'm concerned, is not a very good vetting process since &quot;I'm a native speaker from that region&quot; is apparently not sufficient a vetting process. And frankly, it's a fool's errand for such a small amount of work. <br /> <br /> We try. We do. But there's only so much we can do before it becomes way more trouble than it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:13:39-07:00","id":124618,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is a errata but ...<br /> Page 23 Earth Wasteland stage four description: &quot;All Atheltics dice pools suffer a -3 penalty, including dodge rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> since GMC update defense is pasive you don't actually have to roll for dodging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2896-nemastoncito","name":"Nemastoncito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:20:48-07:00","id":124625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nemastoncito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/122566-mortal-remains-errata-thread?p=124618#post124618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this is a errata but ...<br /> Page 23 Earth Wasteland stage four description: &quot;All Atheltics dice pools suffer a -3 penalty, including dodge rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> since GMC update defense is pasive you don't actually have to roll for dodging.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the opposite of how that change went. Defense has always been passive, but the GMC update changed Dodging from &quot;double Defense&quot; to &quot;double Defense and roll to negate attack successes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T21:35:21-07:00","id":126440,"title":"","content":"Was it a deliberate choice to leave Prometheans out of the Potency descriptions on p.165, or was their section just overlooked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T21:29:15-07:00","id":127972,"title":"","content":"Page 100, Long Night section<br /> <br /> &quot;Back then, inter-racial tensions were high and the Church's active efforts toward <b>segregating</b> its flock was a big deal;&quot;<br /> <br /> Should be <b>de</b>segregating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out 